# PAN-HARNESS

Pan-harness (Panoramic Harness) is this project's harness: `AGENTS.md` (project, way of working, rules), this file (structure and upkeep) and `pan-harness/` (R16).

## Profile

Profile: live-system={{yes or no}}, code={{yes or no}}, sensitive-data={{secrets, pii, confidential (with +) or none}}

The profile sets the parts of the standard the project needs; the reason: D1.

## Map

Each fact in one place, the other files link to it; all in `pan-harness/`:
- `state.md` — current state, `plan.md` — all open work and dates (both at session start); `handoff.md` — the active large task's state and next step (at session start, when `**Status:** active`).
- `playbooks/large-task.md` — planning and running a large task: questions, criteria, plan, `handoff.md`, budget, usage limit (before planning or resuming one).
- `playbooks/delegation.md` — when to hand work to a sub-agent, its model and effort, the brief and the check of its result (before starting a sub-agent).
- `playbooks/questions.md` — the form of a question to the owner: title, `a)`/`b)` options, one `➡️` recommendation with its reason, numbered blocks, a short question, bold in a long message (before asking the owner a question).
- `playbooks/end-of-task.md` — the end-of-task checklist and journal rules: history entry, `plan.md`, lessons, `.gitignore`, checks, commit, report (at the end of every task).
- `system-map.md` — {{components, outside services, secret names, repo map}} (on "where?" or "how is it built?").
- `runbook.md` — commands, scripts, rules for writing text an agent reads, topic tags, accepted warnings (when a command is needed, before writing such text).
- `playbooks/pan-harness.md` — upkeep with `ph-doctor`: the standard, growth limits, project steps, test questions (before upkeep, on a size warning, before a test).
- Journals: `decisions.md` (D…, "why is it so?"), `feedback.md` (F…, when the reason of a rule is needed), `lessons.md` (L…, before similar work), `history/` (past work by month: when past work is needed).
- `archive/` — superseded decisions, old journal parts (when a journal lacks it); `scripts/` — copies from the skill, run at the end of every task: {{`pan-harness-check.mjs`, `secret-check.mjs` with `secrets` in the profile}}.
- `project/` — the project's own files:
  - {{`project/<file>.md` — what is there (keywords), when to read it}};
  - {{`project/playbooks/` — kinds of task: `<name>` (keywords), …}};
  - {{`project/scripts/` — the project's scripts}}.

